Diagnostic patch for gpui-pre-windows 0.3.8 (Cargo.toml and src/directx_atlas.rs),
which is derived from GPUI (https://github.com/zed-industries/zed, crates/gpui_windows)
and licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Modified for the MATSU Editor PoC, to check
https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/56349#issuecomment-6078561427 by hand.
See docs/upstream/zed-56349.md. Do not use it for anything else.

- Each atlas texture and each tile upload (glyphs and the like) is written to
  atlas-<process ID>.txt in the current directory, with the process's private bytes
  (PrivateUsage) right before and right after the call, the change in KiB, and the sum
  of those changes so far ("?" and "without N unknown" when a query failed). The
  measuring itself (two queries and a file write for each upload) takes time between
  the uploads. With POC_ATLAS_UPLOAD=flush, "after" is after Flush returns, which does
  not wait for the GPU.
- POC_ATLAS_UPLOAD picks the call that uploads a tile. Unset: UpdateSubresource, as in
  GPUI. update1: ID3D11DeviceContext1::UpdateSubresource1 with D3D11_COPY_NO_OVERWRITE.
  flush: UpdateSubresource, then Flush. Each upload line names the call that was made.
- POC_ATLAS_LOG=0 turns the measuring and the file off, to compare the calls without
  that cost.
- Cargo.toml enables the windows crate's Win32_System_ProcessStatus feature for
  K32GetProcessMemoryInfo.

Apply inside a copy of the crate with `git apply` or `patch -p1`.

